    "summary": "Stellar acoustic/electric marathon with soaring Dark Star and The Other One",
    "blurb": "The show delivers flawless acoustic sets that flow into powerful electric jams, highlighted by an inspired Dark Star sequence and tight renditions of Candyman and Friend of the Devil. Jerry’s guitar and vocals soar throughout, backed by a thunderous rhythm section.",
    "review": "May 15 1970 at the Fillmore East stands as one of the band’s most ambitious marathons – two intimate acoustic sets bookended by blistering electric stretches that never lose momentum. The first set rolls through folk‑rock gems like Deep Elem Blues and Uncle John’s Band before giving way to a second set that rockets from the classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue into a thunderous Dark Star, which blossoms into a jubilant Saint Stephen and a rollicking turn on Not Fade Away. The encore’s Cold Jordan showcases Pigpen’s organ tapestry in full glory. Across all recordings Jerry Garcia is repeatedly praised for “outstanding” lead work and even pedal‑steel flourishes, while Phil Lesh lays down a thunderous bass foundation that drives the jams. Bob Weir’s banter and vocal harmonies keep the acoustic numbers grounded, and Mickey Hart’s spacey drumming adds texture to the psychedelic peaks. The pristine soundboard capture (gd70-05-15.early-late.sbd.97.sbeok.shnf) presents crystal‑clear instrument separation, making this a must‑listen for anyone wanting the definitive version of this legendary night.",
